IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pid-rules`
IMPORT `pid-dates`

-- Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 (Cth) -- the questions of the discloser: a current or former public official who
-- has made, or is thinking of making, a disclosure of wrongdoing in the Commonwealth public sector, or who has helped
-- with one as a witness, and who may meet a reprisal for it.
--
-- Based on content from the Federal Register of Legislation: "Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013", Compilation No. 20
-- (4 June 2026), Commonwealth of Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts only. Judgments that belong to an authorised officer, the Ombudsman, the IGIS or a
-- court (reasonable grounds, the public interest, exceptional circumstances, the court being satisfied) are asked as
-- facts: "if it is accepted that ...". Nothing here decides them.

§ `Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 -- my questions as a discloser`

§§ `Am I covered? (ss 26(1)(a), 69, 70)`

@export Am I, or was I, a public official who can make a public interest disclosure under the Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 (Cth) (ss 26(1)(a), 69, 70)? A former public official counts. Judges, Royal Commissioners, members of Parliament and their staff are excluded.
GIVEN `what I am or was` IS A `What I am or was` @desc Which best describes your position now, or when you were a public official? Choose "none of these" if none fits (for example a member of the public or an employee of a business with no Commonwealth contract).
      `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an authorised officer of an agency given you written notice under s 70 that the Act applies to your disclosure as if you had been a public official when you obtained the information?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I a public official who can make a public interest disclosure?` `what I am or was` `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official` MEANS
    `s 26(1)(a) -- the discloser is or has been a public official` `what I am or was` `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official`

§§ `Is it disclosable conduct? (ss 29-33)`

@export Is the wrongdoing I want to report "disclosable conduct" under the Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 (ss 29-33)? Bullying, harassment and other personal work-related conduct is generally not, unless it is a reprisal or significant for an agency; disagreement with government policy is not.
GIVEN `whose conduct it is` IS A `Whose conduct` @desc Whose conduct is it: an agency's; a public official's in connection with their position (for a contractor's employee, only conduct connected with the Commonwealth contract); a public official's outside their position; a contracted service provider's in connection with its Commonwealth contract; or someone else's?
      `what kind of conduct it is` IS A `Kind of conduct` @desc Which best describes the conduct? Choose "none of these" if none fits.
      `it is personal work-related conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it conduct by one public official towards another about the other's engagement, appointment, employment or functions with personal implications for them (for example bullying, harassment, a transfer, promotion, discipline, suspension or termination)?
      `it would be a reprisal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would that personal work-related conduct be a reprisal for a public interest disclosure, or an offence under s 19?
      `it is significant for an agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is accepted that the personal work-related conduct is so significant that it would undermine public confidence in an agency, or has other significant implications for an agency.
      `it is only a disagreement with policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your concern relate only to a Commonwealth Government policy, to action by a Minister, the Speaker or the President of the Senate, or to spending on them, that you disagree with?
      `it is excluded court or tribunal conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it conduct of a judge or magistrate, of court or tribunal staff or members exercising the court's or tribunal's powers, or other court or tribunal conduct that is not purely administrative or that relates to managing or hearing matters?
      `it is proper intelligence agency conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it conduct of an intelligence agency, or one of its officials, in the proper performance of the agency's functions or proper exercise of its powers?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is what I want to report disclosable conduct?` `whose conduct it is` `what kind of conduct it is` `it is personal work-related conduct` `it would be a reprisal` `it is significant for an agency` `it is only a disagreement with policy` `it is excluded court or tribunal conduct` `it is proper intelligence agency conduct` MEANS
    `s 29 -- disclosable conduct` `whose conduct it is` `what kind of conduct it is` `it is personal work-related conduct` `it would be a reprisal` `it is significant for an agency` `it is only a disagreement with policy` `it is excluded court or tribunal conduct` `it is proper intelligence agency conduct`

§§ `Who can I disclose to inside government? (s 34)`

@export Is the person I disclosed to (or plan to disclose to) an "authorised internal recipient" under the Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 (s 34)? An authorised officer is the agency head or someone the head appointed in writing. A supervisor is not an authorised internal recipient but can receive an internal disclosure.
GIVEN `what the conduct relates to` IS A `What the conduct relates to` @desc Which agency's conduct is it (the agency, or someone who belonged to it at the time, engaged in it): an ordinary agency, an intelligence agency (ASIS, ASIO, AGO, DIO, ASD, ONI or the ACIC), the Ombudsman or the IGIS?
      `who I disclosed to` IS A `Who I disclosed to` @desc Who is the recipient? Where more than one fits, choose the first in the list.
      `I believe the Ombudsman should investigate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you believe on reasonable grounds that it would be appropriate for the Ombudsman to investigate?
      `I believe it concerns intelligence functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you believe on reasonable grounds that it relates to action by AUSTRAC, the Department of Home Affairs or the AFP in relation to its intelligence functions?
      `I believe the IGIS should investigate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you believe on reasonable grounds that it would be appropriate for the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security to investigate?
      `some of the information is intelligence information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any of the information intelligence information (s 41: from or about an intelligence agency other than the ACIC, its sources, methods or operations, or sensitive law enforcement information)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the person I disclosed to an authorised internal recipient?` `what the conduct relates to` `who I disclosed to` `I believe the Ombudsman should investigate` `I believe it concerns intelligence functions` `I believe the IGIS should investigate` `some of the information is intelligence information` MEANS
    `s 34 -- an authorised internal recipient` `what the conduct relates to` `who I disclosed to` `I believe the Ombudsman should investigate` `I believe it concerns intelligence functions` `I believe the IGIS should investigate` `some of the information is intelligence information`

§§ `Is my disclosure a public interest disclosure? (ss 26, 28)`

@export Is my disclosure an internal disclosure, a kind of public interest disclosure protected by the Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 (s 26(1) item 1)? It must go to an authorised internal recipient or my supervisor, and must not be made in the course of my ordinary duties.
GIVEN `what I am or was` IS A `What I am or was` @desc Which best describes your position now, or when you were a public official? Choose "none of these" if none fits.
      `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an authorised officer given you written notice under s 70 that the Act applies to your disclosure as if you had been a public official?
      `who I disclosed to` IS A `Who I disclosed to` @desc Who received the disclosure? Where more than one fits, choose the first in the list.
      `what the conduct relates to` IS A `What the conduct relates to` @desc Which agency's conduct is it: an ordinary agency, an intelligence agency, the Ombudsman or the IGIS?
      `I believe the Ombudsman should investigate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you believe on reasonable grounds that it would be appropriate for the Ombudsman to investigate?
      `I believe it concerns intelligence functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you believe on reasonable grounds that it relates to action by AUSTRAC, Home Affairs or the AFP in relation to its intelligence functions?
      `I believe the IGIS should investigate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you believe on reasonable grounds that it would be appropriate for the IGIS to investigate?
      `some of the information is intelligence information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any of the information intelligence information (s 41)?
      `it tends to show disclosable conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information tend to show disclosable conduct, or do you believe on reasonable grounds that it does?
      `I made it in the course of my ordinary functions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the disclosure in the course of performing your ordinary functions as a public official (for example as an auditor or investigator reporting in your job)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my disclosure an internal disclosure?` `what I am or was` `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official` `who I disclosed to` `what the conduct relates to` `I believe the Ombudsman should investigate` `I believe it concerns intelligence functions` `I believe the IGIS should investigate` `some of the information is intelligence information` `it tends to show disclosable conduct` `I made it in the course of my ordinary functions` MEANS
    `s 26(1) item 1 -- an internal disclosure`
        (`s 26(1)(a) -- the discloser is or has been a public official` `what I am or was` `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official`)
        (`s 34 -- an authorised internal recipient` `what the conduct relates to` `who I disclosed to` `I believe the Ombudsman should investigate` `I believe it concerns intelligence functions` `I believe the IGIS should investigate` `some of the information is intelligence information`)
        (`who I disclosed to` EQUALS `my supervisor`)
        `it tends to show disclosable conduct`
        `I made it in the course of my ordinary functions`

@export Is my disclosure an external disclosure, to anyone outside government, protected by the Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 (s 26(1) item 2)? It needs an earlier internal disclosure that was inadequately investigated or not finished in time, and must not be against the public interest or include intelligence information.
GIVEN `what I am or was` IS A `What I am or was` @desc Which best describes your position now, or when you were a public official? Choose "none of these" if none fits.
      `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an authorised officer given you written notice under s 70 that the Act applies to your disclosure as if you had been a public official?
      `who I disclosed to` IS A `Who I disclosed to` @desc Who received the disclosure (for example a journalist or member of Parliament is "anyone else")?
      `it tends to show disclosable conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information tend to show disclosable conduct, or do you believe on reasonable grounds that it does?
      `I made an internal disclosure of it before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you earlier make an internal disclosure of information that consisted of or included what you have now disclosed?
      `I believe the investigation was inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your internal disclosure investigated under Division 2 of Part 3, and do you believe on reasonable grounds that the investigation was inadequate?
      `I believe the response was inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your internal disclosure investigated (under this Act or otherwise), and do you believe on reasonable grounds that the response to the investigation was inadequate?
      `the inadequate response is only action by a Minister or presiding officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only inadequacy you see in the response action taken, being taken or to be taken by a Minister, the Speaker or the President of the Senate (s 26(2A))?
      `the investigation ran past the time limit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a Division 2 investigation required and not completed within the s 52 time limit (90 days plus any extension; see the timing questions)?
      `it is not on balance contrary to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is accepted that the disclosure is not, on balance, contrary to the public interest (weighing the matters in s 26(3)).
      `I disclosed no more than reasonably necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is accepted that you publicly disclosed no more information than reasonably necessary to identify the disclosable conduct.
      `some of the information is intelligence information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any of the information intelligence information (s 41)?
      `some conduct relates to an intelligence agency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does any of the conduct relate to an intelligence agency other than the ACIC?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my disclosure an external disclosure?` `what I am or was` `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official` `who I disclosed to` `it tends to show disclosable conduct` `I made an internal disclosure of it before` `I believe the investigation was inadequate` `I believe the response was inadequate` `the inadequate response is only action by a Minister or presiding officer` `the investigation ran past the time limit` `it is not on balance contrary to the public interest` `I disclosed no more than reasonably necessary` `some of the information is intelligence information` `some conduct relates to an intelligence agency` MEANS
    `s 26(1) item 2 -- an external disclosure`
        (`s 26(1)(a) -- the discloser is or has been a public official` `what I am or was` `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official`)
        (`who I disclosed to` EQUALS `a foreign public official`)
        `it tends to show disclosable conduct`
        `I made an internal disclosure of it before`
        `I believe the investigation was inadequate`
        `I believe the response was inadequate`
        `the inadequate response is only action by a Minister or presiding officer`
        `the investigation ran past the time limit`
        `it is not on balance contrary to the public interest`
        `I disclosed no more than reasonably necessary`
        `some of the information is intelligence information`
        `some conduct relates to an intelligence agency`

@export Is my disclosure an emergency disclosure, to anyone, protected by the Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 (s 26(1) item 3)? It is for a substantial and imminent danger to health, safety or the environment, and needs exceptional circumstances if made without, or ahead of, an internal process.
GIVEN `what I am or was` IS A `What I am or was` @desc Which best describes your position now, or when you were a public official? Choose "none of these" if none fits.
      `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an authorised officer given you written notice under s 70 that the Act applies to your disclosure as if you had been a public official?
      `who I disclosed to` IS A `Who I disclosed to` @desc Who received the disclosure?
      `I believe there is a substantial and imminent danger` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you believe on reasonable grounds that the information concerns a substantial and imminent danger to the health or safety of one or more people, or to the environment?
      `I disclosed no more than needed to alert them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is accepted that you disclosed no more than necessary to alert the recipient to the danger.
      `I made an internal disclosure of it before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you earlier make an internal disclosure of the same information?
      `the investigation of it is complete` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you did: has the investigation of that internal disclosure been completed?
      `there are exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is accepted that exceptional circumstances justify not making an internal disclosure first (or, if you made one, making this disclosure before its investigation was completed).
      `some of the information is intelligence information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any of the information intelligence information (s 41)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my disclosure an emergency disclosure?` `what I am or was` `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official` `who I disclosed to` `I believe there is a substantial and imminent danger` `I disclosed no more than needed to alert them` `I made an internal disclosure of it before` `the investigation of it is complete` `there are exceptional circumstances` `some of the information is intelligence information` MEANS
    `s 26(1) item 3 -- an emergency disclosure`
        (`s 26(1)(a) -- the discloser is or has been a public official` `what I am or was` `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official`)
        (`who I disclosed to` EQUALS `a foreign public official`)
        `I believe there is a substantial and imminent danger`
        `I disclosed no more than needed to alert them`
        `I made an internal disclosure of it before`
        `the investigation of it is complete`
        `there are exceptional circumstances`
        `some of the information is intelligence information`

@export Is what I told a lawyer a legal practitioner disclosure, protected by the Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 (s 26(1) item 4)? It must be to get legal advice or help about a public interest disclosure I made or plan to make.
GIVEN `what I am or was` IS A `What I am or was` @desc Which best describes your position now, or when you were a public official? Choose "none of these" if none fits.
      `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an authorised officer given you written notice under s 70 that the Act applies to your disclosure as if you had been a public official?
      `who I disclosed to` IS A `Who I disclosed to` @desc Who received the disclosure?
      `it was to get advice about a public interest disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you tell them in order to get legal advice or professional help about a public interest disclosure you have made or propose to make?
      `I knew or ought to have known some of it is classified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you know, or should you reasonably have known, that any of the information has a national security or other protective security classification?
      `the lawyer holds the clearance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the lawyer hold the appropriate level of security clearance?
      `some of the information is intelligence information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any of the information intelligence information (s 41)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my disclosure a legal practitioner disclosure?` `what I am or was` `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official` `who I disclosed to` `it was to get advice about a public interest disclosure` `I knew or ought to have known some of it is classified` `the lawyer holds the clearance` `some of the information is intelligence information` MEANS
    `s 26(1) item 4 -- a legal practitioner disclosure`
        (`s 26(1)(a) -- the discloser is or has been a public official` `what I am or was` `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official`)
        (`who I disclosed to` EQUALS `an Australian legal practitioner`)
        `it was to get advice about a public interest disclosure`
        `I knew or ought to have known some of it is classified`
        `the lawyer holds the clearance`
        `some of the information is intelligence information`

@export Is my NACC disclosure (to the National Anti-Corruption Commission under the NACC Act 2022) also a public interest disclosure under the Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 (s 26(1A)), so that its protections apply?
GIVEN `what I am or was` IS A `What I am or was` @desc Which best describes your position now, or when you were a public official? Choose "none of these" if none fits.
      `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an authorised officer given you written notice under s 70 that the Act applies to your disclosure as if you had been a public official?
      `it tends to show disclosable conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information tend to show disclosable conduct, or do you believe on reasonable grounds that it does?
      `it is a NACC disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a NACC disclosure as the National Anti-Corruption Commission Act 2022 defines it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my NACC disclosure also a public interest disclosure?` `what I am or was` `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official` `it tends to show disclosable conduct` `it is a NACC disclosure` MEANS
    `s 26(1A) -- a NACC disclosure that is a public interest disclosure`
        (`s 26(1)(a) -- the discloser is or has been a public official` `what I am or was` `an authorised officer determined I am treated as a public official`)
        `it tends to show disclosable conduct`
        `it is a NACC disclosure`

@export Can my public interest disclosure be made orally, anonymously, or without saying it is made under the Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 (s 28)? Not answered for a NACC disclosure, which the NACC Act governs.
GIVEN `it is also a NACC disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure also a NACC disclosure under the National Anti-Corruption Commission Act 2022?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I disclose orally or anonymously or without mentioning the Act?` `it is also a NACC disclosure` MEANS
    `s 28 -- the form does not matter` `it is also a NACC disclosure`

§§ `Am I protected from liability? (ss 10-12B)`

@export Am I protected from this kind of liability for making a public interest disclosure under the Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 (ss 10-12)? Protection covers liability, discipline, contract remedies and defamation, but not knowingly false statements, certain Criminal Code offences, knowingly breaching a publication restriction without excuse, or my own wrongdoing.
GIVEN `my disclosure is a public interest disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your disclosure a public interest disclosure (internal, external, emergency, legal practitioner, or a NACC disclosure that qualifies; see the questions above)?
      `the liability I face` IS A `Liability faced` @desc What are you facing, or worried about facing, because of the disclosure?
      `I knew it breached a publication restriction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a designated publication restriction (for example a Family Court publication ban or a suppression order): did you know the disclosure contravened it?
      `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a designated publication restriction: did you have a reasonable excuse for contravening it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I protected from this liability for my disclosure?` `my disclosure is a public interest disclosure` `the liability I face` `I knew it breached a publication restriction` `I had a reasonable excuse` MEANS
    `ss 10-12 -- the discloser is protected` `my disclosure is a public interest disclosure` `the liability I face` `I knew it breached a publication restriction` `I had a reasonable excuse`

@export As a witness who helped with someone else's public interest disclosure, am I protected from this kind of liability for the help I gave (Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 ss 12A, 12B)?
GIVEN `I made the disclosure myself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the person who made the disclosure (if so, use the discloser's question instead)?
      `the disclosure is a public interest disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the disclosure you helped with a public interest disclosure?
      `I gave information or a document or answered a question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give information, produce a document or other thing, or answer a question?
      `I considered it relevant on reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you consider, on reasonable grounds, that it was relevant to deciding how the disclosure is allocated, to an investigation of it, or to an Ombudsman or IGIS review of how it was handled?
      `the liability I face` IS A `Liability faced` @desc What are you facing, or worried about facing, because of the help you gave?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`As a witness am I protected from this liability?` `I made the disclosure myself` `the disclosure is a public interest disclosure` `I gave information or a document or answered a question` `I considered it relevant on reasonable grounds` `the liability I face` MEANS
    `ss 12A, 12B -- the witness is protected` `I made the disclosure myself` `the disclosure is a public interest disclosure` `I gave information or a document or answered a question` `I considered it relevant on reasonable grounds` `the liability I face`

-- Situation: someone did, or threatened, something against me after a disclosure. Ask "Has this happened to you?" first.
§§ `Reprisals (ss 13-19, 22A)`

@export Has someone taken a reprisal against me under the Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 (s 13)? A reprisal is causing or threatening detriment because they believe or suspect that I or anyone else made, may have made, plans to make or could make a public interest disclosure. No disclosure need actually have been made.
GIVEN `it caused me detriment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did their conduct cause you detriment (for example dismissal, injury in your employment, an adverse change to your position, discrimination, harassment, intimidation, psychological or other harm, or damage to your property, reputation, business or finances)?
      `it threatened me with detriment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did their conduct consist of, or result in, a threat to cause you detriment?
      `they believed or suspected a disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc At the time, did they believe or suspect that you or someone else had made, may have made, proposed to make or could make a public interest disclosure?
      `that was at least part of their reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that belief or suspicion the reason, or part of the reason, for what they did?
      `it was reasonable action to protect me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is accepted that what they did was administrative action reasonable to protect you from detriment (for example moving you away from the people you reported).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Has someone taken a reprisal against me?` `it caused me detriment` `it threatened me with detriment` `they believed or suspected a disclosure` `that was at least part of their reason` `it was reasonable action to protect me` MEANS
    `s 13 -- a reprisal taken against me` `it caused me detriment` `it threatened me with detriment` `they believed or suspected a disclosure` `that was at least part of their reason` `it was reasonable action to protect me`

@export What can the Federal Court or the Federal Circuit and Family Court order for a reprisal taken against me under the Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 (ss 14-17, 22A)? Each order is in the court's discretion. An application under the Fair Work Act about the same conduct bars an application here.
GIVEN `the court is satisfied of the reprisal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the court is satisfied that the person you apply against took, or is taking, a reprisal against you.
      `they acted as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did they take the reprisal in connection with their position as an employee (for example a manager acting for the agency)?
      `their employer took reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If their employer proves that it took reasonable precautions, and exercised due diligence, to avoid the reprisal.
      `I am or was employed by them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are or were you employed in a particular position by the person you apply against?
      `the reprisal included ending my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the reprisal consist wholly or partly of their terminating, or purporting to terminate, your employment?
      `I applied under the Fair Work Act for the same conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied under s 539 of the Fair Work Act 2009 (for a contravention of s 340 or 772) or under s 394 (unfair dismissal) about the same conduct?
      `that application ended without a decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: was that application discontinued, or did it fail for want of jurisdiction?
GIVETH A LIST OF `Order for a reprisal`
`What can the court order for the reprisal against me?` `the court is satisfied of the reprisal` `they acted as an employee` `their employer took reasonable precautions` `I am or was employed by them` `the reprisal included ending my employment` `I applied under the Fair Work Act for the same conduct` `that application ended without a decision` MEANS
    `ss 14-16 -- the orders the court may make` `the court is satisfied of the reprisal` `they acted as an employee` `their employer took reasonable precautions` `I am or was employed by them` `the reprisal included ending my employment` `I applied under the Fair Work Act for the same conduct` `that application ended without a decision`

@export Can I be ordered to pay the other side's costs in my reprisal case under the Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 (s 18)? Only if the court finds I brought it vexatiously or without reasonable cause, or my unreasonable act or omission caused the costs.
GIVEN `the court finds I brought it vexatiously or without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the court is satisfied that you started the proceedings vexatiously or without reasonable cause.
      `the court finds my unreasonable conduct caused the costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the court is satisfied that an unreasonable act or omission of yours caused the other party to incur the costs.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I be ordered to pay the other side's costs?` `the court finds I brought it vexatiously or without reasonable cause` `the court finds my unreasonable conduct caused the costs` MEANS
    `s 18 -- I may be ordered to pay costs` `the court finds I brought it vexatiously or without reasonable cause` `the court finds my unreasonable conduct caused the costs`

@export What is the most a person can be sentenced to for a reprisal, for revealing or using my identity as a discloser, or for a lawyer misusing what I told them, under the Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 (ss 19, 20, 67)? Imprisonment, a fine in penalty units, or both.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc Which offence?
GIVETH A `Maximum penalty`
`What is the most they can be sentenced to?` `the offence` MEANS
    `the maximum penalty for` `the offence`

§§ `My identity (s 20)`

@export Would it be an offence for someone to reveal or use information that identifies me as the person who made a public interest disclosure (Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 s 20)? Several exceptions apply, including my consent and earlier lawful publication.
GIVEN `I made a public interest disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a public interest disclosure?
      `what they did with it` IS A `What they did with it` @desc What did they do with the information: disclose it to someone other than you, disclose it only to you, or use it?
      `it was obtained by a public official` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the information obtained by someone in their capacity as a public official?
      `it is likely to identify me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information likely to enable you to be identified as a person who made a public interest disclosure?
      `the exception that applies` IS AN `Exception that applies` @desc Does one of these exceptions apply? Choose "no exception" if none does.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Would revealing or using information that identifies me be an offence?` `I made a public interest disclosure` `what they did with it` `it was obtained by a public official` `it is likely to identify me` `the exception that applies` MEANS
    `s 20 -- an identifying information offence` `I made a public interest disclosure` `what they did with it` `it was obtained by a public official` `it is likely to identify me` `the exception that applies`

-- Situation: an internal disclosure has been made to an authorised officer (or passed on by a supervisor).
§§ `What happens to my disclosure, and when (ss 43, 52)`

@export By when should the authorised officer decide which agency will handle my internal disclosure (Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 s 43(11))? The officer must use best endeavours to decide within 14 days; the Act sets no consequence for missing it.
GIVEN `the day the period starts` IS A DATE @desc The day you made the disclosure to an authorised officer (or your supervisor gave it to one), or the later day the period restarts from (a recommendation from the Ombudsman or the IGIS received, or a NACC stop action direction known to have ended).
GIVETH A DATE
`By when should my disclosure be allocated?` `the day the period starts` MEANS
    `s 43(11) -- the allocation decision is aimed for by` `the day the period starts`

@export By when must the investigation of my disclosure be completed (Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 s 52)? 90 days after allocation, reallocation or a decision to reinvestigate, plus any extension the Ombudsman or the IGIS grants. A weekend or public holiday does not move the day here.
GIVEN `the day the period starts` IS A DATE @desc The day your disclosure was allocated (or reallocated, or the principal officer decided to reinvestigate it, or became aware a NACC stop action direction no longer applied).
      `extension in days` IS A NUMBER @desc Total days of extension the Ombudsman or the IGIS has granted (0 if none). You can apply for one yourself.
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the investigation be completed?` `the day the period starts` `extension in days` MEANS
    `s 52 -- the investigation must be completed by` `the day the period starts` `extension in days`

@export Was the investigation of my disclosure completed within the time limit (Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 s 52)? If not, an external disclosure can meet item 2(c)(iii) of s 26(1); the investigation itself stays valid (s 52(6)).
GIVEN `the day the period starts` IS A DATE @desc The day your disclosure was allocated (or reallocated, or the principal officer decided to reinvestigate it, or became aware a NACC stop action direction no longer applied).
      `extension in days` IS A NUMBER @desc Total days of extension the Ombudsman or the IGIS has granted (0 if none).
      `the report has been prepared` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the principal officer prepared the report of the investigation (that is when it is completed, s 52(2))?
      `the day the report was prepared` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day it was prepared (any date if not).
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about, usually today.
GIVETH AN `Investigation timing`
`Was the investigation completed within the time limit?` `the day the period starts` `extension in days` `the report has been prepared` `the day the report was prepared` `the day I am asking about` MEANS
    `s 52 -- how the investigation stands` `the day the period starts` `extension in days` `the report has been prepared` `the day the report was prepared` `the day I am asking about`
